      <Item ItemId=";Visual_Long_Description" ItemType="0" PsrId="306" Leaf="true">
        <Str Cat="Text">
          <Val><![CDATA[Tornado charts are a special type of bar chart where the data categories are listed vertically instead of the standard horizontal presentation, and the categories are ordered so that the largest bar appears at the top of the chart, the second largest appears second from the top, and so on. They are so named because the final chart visually resembles either one half of or a complete tornado.]A;A tornado chart is a common tool used to depict the sensitivity of a result to changes in selected variables. It shows the effect on the output of varying each input variable at a time, keeping all the other input variables at their initial (nominal) values. Typically, you choose a “low” and a “high” value for each input.]A;This is an open source visual. Get the code from GitHub: https://github.com/Microsoft/PowerBI-visuals-tornado]]></Val>
          <Tgt Cat="Text" Stat="Loc" Orig="New">
            <Val><![CDATA[龍捲風圖是一種特殊的橫條圖，其中資料類別會垂直列出，而不是標準的水平呈現，而且類別會依序排列，因此最大的橫條會顯示在圖表最上方，第二大則顯示在從上方數來第二個位置，以此類推。最終圖表看起來會像是一半或完整的龍捲風，便依此為圖表命名。]A;要說明選擇的變數經過變化後的敏感度時，常會使用龍捲風圖。它會顯示每次改變各輸入變數的輸出效果，其他所有輸入變數則會保持初始 (名目) 值。通常，會為各輸入選擇「低」和「高」值。]A;這是一種開放原始碼視覺效果。從 GitHub 取得程式碼: https://github.com/Microsoft/PowerBI-visuals-tornado]]></Val>
          </Tgt>
          <Prev Cat="Text">
            <Val><![CDATA[Tornado charts, are a special type of Bar chart, where the data categories are listed vertically instead of the standard horizontal presentation, and the categories are ordered so that the largest bar appears at the top of the chart, the second largest appears second from the top, and so on. They are so named because the final chart visually resembles either one half of or a complete tornado.]A;A tornado chart is a common tool used to depict the sensitivity of a result to changes in selected variables. It shows the effect on the output of varying each input variable at a time, keeping all the other input variables at their initial (nominal) values. Typically, you choose a “low” and a “high” value for each input.]A;This is an open source visual. Get the code from GitHub: https://github.com/Microsoft/PowerBI-visuals-tornado]]></Val>
          </Prev>
        </Str>
        <Disp Icon="Str" />
      </Item>
